  "description": "extending our conservatory by adding a Decking at the same level as our conservatory door which leads to a set of stairs and rockery which lead down to the garden. Both stairs and the rockery represent a serious risk of harm as our mobility/stability has declined with our age (we are both 70 years old with health issues), thus putting us more at risk of falling. Without this work being carried out we would not have access to our own garden. \nWe were advised we would not need planning permission as our conservatory itself overlooks our neighbours garden. The deck itself is not an extension of the conservatory and it is as the exact same level as our conservatory back door. \nNow we have received a letter from Mr. Amauni Campbell, Planning Enforcement order. We would like to apply for a retrospective planning application.",
